# 🔟 Strongly Connected Components (SCC)

## Definition

In Directed Graph:

Every node can reach every other node.

---

### Example

```text
1 → 2

↑   ↓

4 ← 3
```

All nodes connected mutually.

One SCC.

---

# 1️⃣1️⃣ Kosaraju Algorithm

Used to find:

```text
All SCCs
```

---

### Steps

#### Step 1

Topological Order using DFS.

---

#### Step 2

Reverse Graph.

---

#### Step 3

Process nodes in reverse finishing order.

---

Each DFS gives:

```text
One SCC
```

---

# 1️⃣2️⃣ Kosaraju Code Skeleton

```cpp
dfs1(node);

store in stack;

reverse graph;

while(!stack.empty())
{
    node = stack.top();

    if(not visited)
    {
        dfs2(node);

        SCC++;
    }
}
```

---

### Complexity

```text
O(V + E)
```

---

# 1️⃣3️⃣ Bridges in Graph

## Definition

An edge whose removal increases:

```text
Connected Components
```

---

### Example

```text
1 --- 2 --- 3
```

Remove:

```text
2---3
```

Graph disconnects.

Bridge found.

---

# 1️⃣4️⃣ Tarjan's Concept

Maintain:

```cpp
tin[]
```

and

```cpp
low[]
```

---

### Meaning

```text
tin[node]
```

Time of first visit.

---

```text
low[node]
```

Lowest reachable time.

---

### Bridge Condition

```cpp
if(
low[child]
>
tin[parent]
)
```

Then:

```text
Bridge Exists
```

---

# 1️⃣5️⃣ Bridge Detection DFS

```cpp
dfs(node,parent)
{
    vis[node]=1;

    tin[node]=low[node]=timer++;

    for(neighbor)
    {
        if(neighbor==parent)
            continue;

        if(!vis[neighbor])
        {
            dfs(neighbor,node);

            low[node] =
            min(
                low[node],
                low[neighbor]
            );

            if(
                low[neighbor]
                >
                tin[node]
            )
            {
                // Bridge
            }
        }
        else
        {
            low[node] =
            min(
                low[node],
                tin[neighbor]
            );
        }
    }
}
```

---

### Complexity

```text
O(V + E)
```

---

# 1️⃣6️⃣ Articulation Point

## Definition

A vertex whose removal increases:

```text
Connected Components
```

---

### Example

```text
1

|

2

/ \

3 4
```

Remove:

```text
2
```

Graph breaks.

Articulation Point:

```text
2
```

---

# 1️⃣7️⃣ Condition

For non-root node:

```cpp
low[child]
>=
tin[node]
```

---

Then:

```text
Node is Articulation Point
```

---

### Root Node

Must have:

```text
More Than One Child
```

---

# 1️⃣8️⃣ Complexity

```text
Time: O(V + E)

Space: O(V)
```

